From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Velez Garcia <velezgarciaemmanuel25@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 22:19:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Write player data on a background queue

An autosave calls savePlayers(), which writes an NBT file for every online
player back to back in a single tick. With a few hundred players that
stalls the server for as long as the disk takes.

The compound is still built on the main thread, so what gets written is
the state at the moment of the save; only the write is handed to a single
writer thread. That thread keeps writes for the same file in submission
order, so a later save can never be overwritten by an earlier one, and
data still sitting in the queue is readable, so a player who reconnects
before their save flushed reads their newest inventory rather than what is
on disk. The queue is drained before the server stops.

Controlled by saving.asyncPlayerData, on by default.

